/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate18_nrtl_isopropanol_dimethylCarbonate -- AN NRTL PAIR FROM PUBLISHED MEASUREMENTS, BY THE PIPELINE.

  WRITTEN BY bin/choupo-curate pair isopropanol dimethylCarbonate (DEV.md 4c C282; record
  docs/design/binary-pairs-from-open-measurements.md section 8).  Every rule
  below was decided before this tool existed (C16, C225, C226); the tool
  applies them and decides nothing.

  @@PILOT-BEGIN@@
  WHY THIS PAIR -- THE PILOT RANKING (C282; added after the run, but the
  ranking reads ONLY the archive index and was computed before any fit).
  Candidates: both components in the catalogue, NO record for the pair in
  any model directory of data/standards/parameters/, no acetic acid (vapour
  dimerisation, C16), no component whose vapour pressure is AmbroseWalton
  (C281), and (checked for the five chosen) no binary block in the archive
  with a second liquid.  Ranked
  by the number of mutually author-disjoint isobaric bubble-T studies at or
  below 110 kPa with a declared uncertainty, then by their total points:
     1 methanol + dimethylCarbonate        5 independent (9 studies, 274 pts)
     - acetone + methanol                  4 -- passed over: curate05 holds
                                             its C16 regression and the two
                                             studies' disagreement, a
                                             curator's tie-break
     2 ethanol + dimethylCarbonate         4 (4 studies, 156 pts)
     3 diisopropylEther + isopropanol      3 (4 studies, 152 pts)
     - triethyleneGlycol + water           3 -- REFUSED by the tool: 2 of 3
                                             studies disagree beyond their U
     4 isopropanol + dimethylCarbonate     3 (3 studies, 128 pts)
     - 2Butanol + dimethylCarbonate        3 -- REFUSED by the tool: no
                                             author-disjoint held-out study
                                             reports x of the same component
     5 ethanol + 224Trimethylpentane       3 (5 studies, 97 pts)
  THIS CASE: rank 4.
  @@PILOT-END@@

  THE DECLARATION -- WRITTEN AND COMMITTED BEFORE ANY FIT RAN.
  (C16 slice 2: so the declaration can be read against the result.)

  IDENTITY.  isopropanol (CAS 67-63-0, InChIKey KFZMGEQAYNKOFK-UHFFFAOYSA-N)
  + dimethylCarbonate (CAS 616-38-6, InChIKey IEJIGPNLZYLLBP-UHFFFAOYSA-N), joined
  to the archive through identity.json -- never by name.

  NO MEASURED SERIES IN THIS TREE.  constant/archiveDatasets names each
  dataset (DOI, NIST URL, article sha256, extraction selector, extract
  sha256); `bin/choupo-curate fetch` writes the points into
  constant/archiveExtracts/, which is gitignored.

  STUDIES CONSIDERED: every bubble-temperature block of the pair at or below
  110 kPa with a declared uncertainty (3 block(s)).
  USABLE after the screens: 2.  SET ASIDE, BY NAME:
      - doi 10.1016/j.jct.2011.08.006 block 6: TRIAGE: disagrees with the
      other studies beyond their stated uncertainties
      (leave-one-study-out, below)

  TRIAGE (C226 item 3, leave one study out, fitted by the engine; a study
  whose held-out AAD exceeds its own largest stated U plus the others'
  largest stated U disagrees with them beyond their stated uncertainties):
      10.1016/j.jct.2011.08.006: AAD 0.636 K against the limit 0.520 K ->
      DISAGREES -- set aside; 10.1016/j.jct.2004.09.009: AAD 0.629 K
      against the limit 0.670 K -> agrees; 10.1021/je030131q: AAD 0.578 K
      against the limit 0.670 K -> agrees

  PARTITION (the declared rule of C16 slice 2): the FIT set is the usable
  study with the most interior points; the HELD-OUT set is the next largest
  that shares NO author with it and was measured at one pressure.
    FIT       doi 10.1016/j.jct.2004.09.009 (32 interior points, 101.3 kPa)
              authors: Pereiro, A. B.; Rodriguez, A.; Canosa, J.; Tojo, J.
    HELD OUT  doi 10.1021/je030131q (9 interior points, 95.8 kPa)
              authors: Vittal Prasad, T. E.; Prashanth, P. R.; Kumar, D. S.; Prasad, D.H.L.

  BAND: maxAAD 0.24 % of the held-out mean T.
      declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate, the ONE rule of C16:
      the held-out set's largest stated expanded uncertainty (U95 = 0.32
      K) plus the catalogue vapour-pressure model's own error at that
      set's pure endpoints (dimethylCarbonate +0.504 K, isopropanol
      -0.231 K; measured with no pair involved), as a percentage of the
      held-out mean T (351.83 K) = 0.2341 %, rounded UP to two
      significant figures

  THE FIT.  NRTL with a_ij = a_ji = 0 and alpha = 0.30 fixed: TWO parameters
  (b_ij, b_ji), the C16 frame (bubble temperatures over these ranges do not
  identify more).  Each point weighted by 1/U, U its own stated expanded
  uncertainty.  Two starts: (0, 0) and (800, -400).

  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  fit_nrtl: b_ij = 284.4 K, b_ji = 62.9 K, in-sample rms 0.132 K over 32
  points; fit_nrtl_start2 lands on the same pair (284.4, 62.9). HELD OUT:
  AAD 0.184 K (0.0521 %) against the band 0.24 % -> validated. PROMOTED
  on 2026-11-10 into
  data/standards/parameters/NRTL/dimethylCarbonate-isopropanol.dat as
  reviewStatus autoPromoted, humanReviewed false, because: verdict
  validated, one liquid across the validity span, triage run
  @@RESULT-END@@

  WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED.  The pair is correct at these pressures and in this
  frame (ideal-gas vapour, the catalogue's own vapour-pressure records); the
  measurements were transcribed by the archive and have NOT been read back
  against the articles (the CHECKLIST that `fetch` writes beside the extracts
  is the aid for that reading).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name        fit_nrtl;
        type        fitParameters;

        parameters
        (
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.isopropanol-dimethylCarbonate.b_ij;  initial 0;  min -3000;  max 3000; }
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.isopropanol-dimethylCarbonate.b_ji;  initial 0;  min -3000;  max 3000; }
        );

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset  "constant/archiveExtracts/isopropanol-dimethylCarbonate-bubble-j.jct.2004.09.009.dat";
                role     fit;
            }
            {
                dataset  "constant/archiveExtracts/isopropanol-dimethylCarbonate-bubble-je030131q.dat";
                role     validation;
            }
        );

        acceptance
        {
            maxAAD  0.24 percent;
            origin  "declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate, the ONE rule of C16: the held-out set's largest stated expanded uncertainty (U95 = 0.32 K) plus the catalogue vapour-pressure model's own error at that set's pure endpoints (dimethylCarbonate +0.504 K, isopropanol -0.231 K; measured with no pair involved), as a percentage of the held-out mean T (351.83 K) = 0.2341 %, rounded UP to two significant figures";
        }

        objective { method leastSquares; }
        residual
        {
            kind        T_bubble;
            components  ( isopropanol dimethylCarbonate );
            weighting   uncertainty;
        }

        options
        {
            maxIter      80;
            tolerance    1.0e-6;
            fdStep       1.0e-4;
            lambda0      1.0e-3;
        }

        output
        {
            fit_log    fit_history.csv;
            parity     parity.csv;
            proposal   dimethylCarbonate-isopropanol.proposal.dat;
        }
    }
    {
        name        fit_nrtl_start2;
        type        fitParameters;

        parameters
        (
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.isopropanol-dimethylCarbonate.b_ij;  initial 800;  min -3000;  max 3000; }
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.isopropanol-dimethylCarbonate.b_ji;  initial -400;  min -3000;  max 3000; }
        );

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset  "constant/archiveExtracts/isopropanol-dimethylCarbonate-bubble-j.jct.2004.09.009.dat";
                role     fit;
            }
            {
                dataset  "constant/archiveExtracts/isopropanol-dimethylCarbonate-bubble-je030131q.dat";
                role     validation;
            }
        );

        acceptance
        {
            maxAAD  0.24 percent;
            origin  "declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate, the ONE rule of C16: the held-out set's largest stated expanded uncertainty (U95 = 0.32 K) plus the catalogue vapour-pressure model's own error at that set's pure endpoints (dimethylCarbonate +0.504 K, isopropanol -0.231 K; measured with no pair involved), as a percentage of the held-out mean T (351.83 K) = 0.2341 %, rounded UP to two significant figures";
        }

        objective { method leastSquares; }
        residual
        {
            kind        T_bubble;
            components  ( isopropanol dimethylCarbonate );
            weighting   uncertainty;
        }

        options
        {
            maxIter      80;
            tolerance    1.0e-6;
            fdStep       1.0e-4;
            lambda0      1.0e-3;
        }

        output
        {
            parity     parity_start2.csv;
        }
    }
    {
        name        txy_ideal;
        type        propertyScan1D;
        vary        { variable x[isopropanol];  from 0.0;  to 1.0;  n 101; }
        state       { P 95.8 kPa;  composition { isopropanol 0.5;  dimethylCarbonate 0.5; } }
        thermo
        {
            equilibrium { liquid { activityModel { model ideal; } } }
        }
        properties  ( T_bubble  y_eq_isopropanol );
        output      { file txy_ideal.csv; }
    }
    {
        name        txy_nrtl;
        type        propertyScan1D;
        vary        { variable x[isopropanol];  from 0.0;  to 1.0;  n 101; }
        state       { P 95.8 kPa;  composition { isopropanol 0.5;  dimethylCarbonate 0.5; } }
        thermo
        {
